crL(){return A.fm(!0,"Rendering",A.a([A.aH(new A.bDR(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/text_example.dart","    In this example we show different ways of rendering text.\n  ","Text"),A.aH(new A.bDS(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/isometric_tile_map_example.dart","    Shows an example of how to use the `IsometricTileMapComponent`.\n\n\n    Move the mouse over the board to see a selector appearing on the tiles.\n  ","Isometric Tile Map"),A.aH(new A.bDT(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/culling_example.dart",'The camera slowly moves over a big field of animated sprites. Only a few of\nthem are on-screen at any time. Press C, or use the "Culled" knob, to turn\n`CullWhenOffscreen` on and off. Compare the frame rate and the number of\nsprites that are drawn on each frame.\n\nThe "Sprites" knob changes how many sprites there are, and the "Camera speed"\nknob how fast the camera moves.\n  ',"Culling"),A.aH(new A.bDU(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/culling_visualized_example.dart",'See which sprites `CullWhenOffscreen` skips. The big view shows the whole field.\nThe small view in the bottom right corner is a second camera that moves around,\nand it is the one that does the culling. The white box shows what it sees.\n\nA sprite is bright in the big view if the small camera drew it, and dim if the\nsmall camera skipped it.\n\nPress C, or use the "Culled" knob, to turn culling on and off. With culling on,\nonly the sprites near the white box are bright. With culling off, the small\ncamera draws every sprite, so all of them are bright.\n\nThe FPS at the top is for the whole game. While the big view is on, it sets the\nFPS, because it always draws every sprite. Press V, or use the "Big view" knob,\nto hide the big view. Then the FPS is the FPS of the small camera alone.\n\nThe "Sprites" knob changes how many sprites there are, and the "Camera speed"\nknob how fast the small camera moves.\n\nThe "draw time" line is how long the small camera needs to draw its sprites in\nDart. It does not include the work of the GPU.\n  ',"Culling (visualized)"),A.aH(new A.bDV(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/nine_tile_box_example.dart","    If you want to create a background for something that can stretch you can\n    use the `NineTileBox` which is showcased here.\n\n\n    Tap to make the box bigger and double tap to make it smaller.\n  ","Nine Tile Box"),A.aH(new A.bDW(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/flip_sprite_example.dart","    In this example we show how you can flip components horizontally and\n    vertically.\n  ","Flip Sprite"),A.aH(new A.bDX(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/layers_example.dart","    In this example we show how layers can be used to produce a shadow effect.\n  ","Layers"),A.aH(new A.bDY(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/particles_example.dart","    Showcases the declarative particle system. Every effect is built from\n    ParticleEmitterComponents: reusable ParticleEmitter presets describe what\n    to spawn (rate, bursts, shapes, velocities) and how particles evolve\n    (gravity, drag, scale, opacity and color over life), while renderers draw\n    all particles of an emitter in a single batched draw call. Watch the\n    live particle counter: everything runs from preallocated buffers.\n  ","Particles"),A.aH(new A.bDZ(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/particles_interactive_example.dart","Drag around the canvas to paint with particles, and pick an effect in the knobs panel to try the different emitter presets and renderers. A single pooled ParticleEmitterComponent follows the pointer: worldSpace keeps already-spawned particles in place while emit() releases more from the preallocated buffer, so no objects are allocated while you draw.","Particles (Interactive)"),A.aH(new A.bE_(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/rich_text_example.dart","A non-interactive example of how to render rich text in Flame.","Rich Text"),A.aH(new A.bE0(),"https://github.com/flame-engine/flame/blob/main/examples/lib/stories/rendering/text_box_example.dart","TextBoxComponent reflows text when boxConfig.maxWidth is changed","TextBoxComponent")],t.l))},
